  "ssml": "<speak version=\"1.0\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis\" xmlns:mstts=\"https://www.w3.org/2001/mstts\" xml:lang=\"en-PH\">\n  <voice name=\"en-PH-JamesNeural\">\n    <mstts:express-as style=\"friendly\">\n      <prosody rate=\"95%\" pitch=\"+2%\">\n        Look at how our local culture fits every <phoneme alphabet=\"ipa\" ph=\"əˈnælədʒi\">analogy</phoneme> rule. <break time=\"550ms\"/> The <emphasis level=\"moderate\">pygmy</emphasis> bonsai trees on Mount <phoneme alphabet=\"ipa\" ph=\"hɑːmiˈɡiːtɑːn\">Hamiguitan</phoneme> give us Synonyms: <emphasis level=\"moderate\">pygmy</emphasis> is to <emphasis level=\"moderate\">dwarf</emphasis>, <break time=\"300ms\"/> as ancient is to old. <break time=\"550ms\"/> And in <phoneme alphabet=\"ipa\" ph=\"mɑːnˈdɑːjɑː\"><emphasis level=\"moderate\">Mandaya</emphasis></phoneme> villages near <phoneme alphabet=\"ipa\" ph=\"ɑːliˈwɑːɡwɑːɡ\"><emphasis level=\"moderate\">Aliwagwag</emphasis></phoneme> Falls in <phoneme alphabet=\"ipa\" ph=\"kɑːtɛˈɛl\"><emphasis level=\"moderate\">Cateel</emphasis></phoneme>, <break time=\"300ms\"/> a single abaca fiber is woven into sacred <phoneme alphabet=\"ipa\" ph=\"dɑːɡˈmaɪ\"><emphasis level=\"moderate\">Dagmay</emphasis></phoneme> cloth. <break time=\"550ms\"/> Abaca fiber is to <phoneme alphabet=\"ipa\" ph=\"dɑːɡˈmaɪ\"><emphasis level=\"moderate\">Dagmay</emphasis></phoneme> cloth, <break time=\"300ms\"/> as coral is to <phoneme alphabet=\"ipa\" ph=\"puːˈhɑːdɑː\">Pujada</phoneme> Reef!\n      </prosody>\n    </mstts:express-as>\n  </voice>\n</speak>",
